66
00:03:06,590 --> 00:03:09,490
Page two: Defining the gameplay within the social context.

67
00:03:09,490 --> 00:03:11,480
Then, let's look at the subtitle.

68
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:13,360
So, I defined this gameplay concept under two specific conditions.

69
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:16,880
First, the gameplay must provide value to the user.

70
00:03:16,880 --> 00:03:18,180
That's what will get users to actually want to play.

71
00:03:18,180 --> 00:03:19,940
This is especially true for English learning products.

72
00:03:19,940 --> 00:03:23,600
Second, the gameplay has to tie into Lili Speaking's core competitive advantage.

73
00:03:23,600 --> 00:03:25,180
which is learning spoken language.

74
00:03:25,180 --> 00:03:28,160
So, for my part, I proposed a real-person conversation feature.

75
00:03:28,160 --> 00:03:30,709
So, where did this idea for the gameplay come from?

76
00:03:30,869 --> 00:03:32,869
And that's when it reminded me of my elementary school days.

77
00:03:32,869 --> 00:03:35,000
we were rehearsing an English play in class.

78
00:03:35,320 --> 00:03:37,660
So, drawing from that experience, I came up with an idea.

79
00:03:37,660 --> 00:03:40,190
So, I thought, could we do something similar within an app?

80
00:03:40,190 --> 00:03:43,350
You could match with strangers online,

81
00:03:43,350 --> 00:03:45,170
and then do some role-playing.

82
00:03:45,170 --> 00:03:47,050
and practice speaking with them.

83
00:03:47,050 --> 00:03:49,530
So, there are scripts and lines to follow.

84
00:03:49,530 --> 00:03:52,760
This way, it also prevents that awkward moment when you're matched with a real person,

85
00:03:52,760 --> 00:03:55,420
and that awkward situation where you don't know what to say.

86
00:03:55,420 --> 00:03:57,980
So, that's why I came up with this real-person conversation feature.

87
00:03:57,980 --> 00:03:59,400
But, by adding a script...

88
00:03:59,400 --> 00:04:02,160
I've talked to a lot of students about putting together their portfolios.

89
00:04:02,160 --> 00:04:04,810
I've noticed that when a lot of people are doing design,

90
00:04:04,810 --> 00:04:08,170
what's in their minds isn't a collection of various methodologies,

91
00:04:08,170 --> 00:04:09,210
or all sorts of industry jargon.

92
00:04:09,210 --> 00:04:09,930
A lot of the time,

93
00:04:09,930 --> 00:04:10,730
A good design,

94
00:04:10,730 --> 00:04:13,600
It comes from something that just suddenly pops into your head.

95
00:04:13,600 --> 00:04:18,240
And that sudden idea? Well, that also comes from your past life experiences.

96
00:04:18,240 --> 00:04:20,120
what you've heard,

97
00:04:20,120 --> 00:04:22,070
And then, at some point, all these little bits and pieces in your head...

98
00:04:22,070 --> 00:04:25,909
And through that one connection, you suddenly get this flash of inspiration.

99
00:04:25,909 --> 00:04:27,909
And then, you come up with a really great idea.

100
00:04:27,909 --> 00:04:29,129
And that's pretty much how it happens.

101
00:04:29,129 --> 00:04:31,589
So, I think you just have to be real and face this process head-on.

102
00:04:31,589 --> 00:04:33,380
Especially in your portfolio.

103
00:04:33,380 --> 00:04:35,160
Of course, I know what a lot of you might be thinking.

104
00:04:35,160 --> 00:04:36,180
So, what if I do it this way?

105
00:04:36,180 --> 00:04:39,220
does that mean I'm not following a standard design process?

106
00:04:39,220 --> 00:04:41,380
Doesn't that make me look unprofessional?

107
00:04:41,380 --> 00:04:42,640
I don't think so.

108
00:04:42,640 --> 00:04:43,900
The real design process

109
00:04:43,900 --> 00:04:46,140
And not many people actually follow a design process in a really rigid, by-the-book way.

110
00:04:46,140 --> 00:04:47,880
to do design.

111
00:04:47,880 --> 00:04:50,159
I think of the design process as a toolbox.

112
00:04:50,159 --> 00:04:52,319
And whether you can actually create a great design in the end...

113
00:04:52,319 --> 00:04:53,839
aren't really that connected.

114
00:04:53,839 --> 00:04:55,930
Or rather, there's no definitive link between the two.

115
00:04:55,930 --> 00:04:59,170
Well, its purpose is to constantly keep you on the right track with your design.

116
00:04:59,170 --> 00:05:02,940
It keeps you on the right track, always moving towards solving the problem.

117
00:05:02,940 --> 00:05:05,220
This might help you avoid some detours.

118
00:05:05,220 --> 00:05:06,260
and cut down on rework.

119
00:05:06,260 --> 00:05:07,940
But for projects that require creativity,

120
00:05:07,940 --> 00:05:09,900
or when you need to come up with gameplay for a C-end product,

121
00:05:09,900 --> 00:05:11,020
And I think that's what makes it so genuine.

122
00:05:11,020 --> 00:05:14,490
and just naturally talk about the process of how that spark of inspiration hit you.

123
00:05:14,490 --> 00:05:16,020
I think that's a great approach.

124
00:05:16,020 --> 00:05:18,820
So you should just talk about it naturally in your portfolio.

125
00:05:18,820 --> 00:05:20,100
And you need to emphasize that point.

126
00:05:20,100 --> 00:05:23,800
That's what shows that this design has a real origin for you.

127
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:26,260
And it's a connection that's uniquely yours.

128
00:05:26,260 --> 00:05:29,420
And it also explains why you were able to create a design like this.

129
00:05:29,420 --> 00:05:30,420
in a way that others can't.

130
00:05:30,420 --> 00:05:34,140
So, there's a connection between your life experiences and your design, right?

131
